{"source":"Pasted text(20261112-150057).txt, first complete copy","governance_item_count":97,"items":[{"source_id":"GOV-02-001","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"This document defines Lumira's final building scope.","source_line":31},{"source_id":"GOV-02-002","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Every numbered requirement and sub-requirement must be accounted for.","source_line":32},{"source_id":"GOV-02-003","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Do not introduce unrelated feature categories.","source_line":33},{"source_id":"GOV-02-004","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Do not remove requirements because they are difficult, expensive or time-consuming.","source_line":34},{"source_id":"GOV-02-005","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Do not silently merge requirements in a way that loses functionality.","source_line":35},{"source_id":"GOV-02-006","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Existing implementations must be inspected and tested before being counted as complete.","source_line":36},{"source_id":"GOV-02-007","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Reuse working existing components where appropriate.","source_line":37},{"source_id":"GOV-02-008","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Fix incomplete implementations instead of unnecessarily duplicating them.","source_line":38},{"source_id":"GOV-02-009","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Do not rewrite stable architecture without a demonstrated engineering reason.","source_line":39},{"source_id":"GOV-02-010","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Preserve backward compatibility wherever reasonably possible.","source_line":40},{"source_id":"GOV-02-011","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Maintain modular architecture and clear separation of responsibilities.","source_line":41},{"source_id":"GOV-02-012","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Follow deterministic orchestration wherever deterministic behavior is required.","source_line":42},{"source_id":"GOV-02-013","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Maintain explicit state tracking throughout workflows.","source_line":43},{"source_id":"GOV-02-014","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"A rejected validation must stop the relevant pipeline.","source_line":44},{"source_id":"GOV-02-015","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Never invent successful test results.","source_line":45},{"source_id":"GOV-02-016","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Never claim that a feature works merely because its files or classes exist.","source_line":46},{"source_id":"GOV-02-017","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Never claim background work continues after the execution session ends.","source_line":47},{"source_id":"GOV-02-018","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Never report a percentage without defining its denominator and verification criteria.","source_line":48},{"source_id":"GOV-02-019","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Do not weaken security controls to make implementation easier.","source_line":49},{"source_id":"GOV-02-020","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Do not use real credentials in source code, tests or logs.","source_line":50},{"source_id":"GOV-02-021","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Do not execute untrusted generated code directly on the host.","source_line":51},{"source_id":"GOV-02-022","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"External services and hardware must be represented as explicit dependencies with integration and acceptance tests.","source_line":52},{"source_id":"GOV-02-023","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Implement meaningful error handling, logging, monitoring and recovery.","source_line":53},{"source_id":"GOV-02-024","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Keep documentation synchronized with actual implementation.","source_line":54},{"source_id":"GOV-02-025","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Maintain a requirement-to-code-to-test traceability record.","source_line":55},{"source_id":"GOV-02-026","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Do not stop at architecture documents or planning. Implement the actual systems.","source_line":56},{"source_id":"GOV-02-027","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Do not declare completion while required functionality remains unimplemented or unverified.","source_line":57},{"source_id":"GOV-02-028","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"When a requirement is blocked by hardware, credentials, provider availability or environment limitations, implement the integration boundary and clearly record the remaining external acceptance test.","source_line":58},{"source_id":"GOV-02-029","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Work in dependency order.","source_line":59},{"source_id":"GOV-02-030","source_section":"GOV-02","source_kind":"development_rule","source_text":"Preserve all user data and existing project history.","source_line":60},{"source_id":"GOV-03-001","source_section":"GOV-03","source_kind":"repository_safety","source_text":"Inspect the complete repository.","source_line":66},{"source_id":"GOV-03-002","source_section":"GOV-03","source_kind":"repository_safety","source_text":"Identify the active branch and current commit.","source_line":67},{"source_id":"GOV-03-003","source_section":"GOV-03","source_kind":"repository_safety","source_text":"Inspect Git status and uncommitted changes.","source_line":68},{"source_id":"GOV-03-004","source_section":"GOV-03","source_kind":"repository_safety","source_text":"Identify the existing architecture, modules, services, APIs, databases and tests.","source_line":69},{"source_id":"GOV-03-005","source_section":"GOV-03","source_kind":"repository_safety","source_text":"Read existing architecture and handoff documentation.","source_line":70},{"source_id":"GOV-03-006","source_section":"GOV-03","source_kind":"repository_safety","source_text":"Identify existing implementations of every requirement in this document.","source_line":71},{"source_id":"GOV-03-007","source_section":"GOV-03","source_kind":"repository_safety","source_text":"Identify incomplete, duplicate, broken and missing components.","source_line":72},{"source_id":"GOV-03-008","source_section":"GOV-03","source_kind":"repository_safety","source_text":"Identify existing security controls and data-protection rules.","source_line":73},{"source_id":"GOV-03-009","source_section":"GOV-03","source_kind":"repository_safety","source_text":"Establish a safe implementation worktree or branch.","source_line":74},{"source_id":"GOV-03-010","source_section":"GOV-03","source_kind":"repository_safety","source_text":"Create a baseline inventory and test report.","source_line":75},{"source_id":"GOV-08-001","source_section":"GOV-08","source_kind":"acceptance_gate","source_text":"**Inventory reconciliation:** Map all 30 previously approved systems, all 99 capability records, all existing registry entries and every requirement in this document.","source_line":1059},{"source_id":"GOV-08-002","source_section":"GOV-08","source_kind":"acceptance_gate","source_text":"**Architecture:** Define each component's responsibility, interfaces and dependencies.","source_line":1060},{"source_id":"GOV-08-003","source_section":"GOV-08","source_kind":"acceptance_gate","source_text":"**Implementation:** Implement every requirement that is not already genuinely implemented.","source_line":1061},{"source_id":"GOV-08-004","source_section":"GOV-08","source_kind":"acceptance_gate","source_text":"**Integration:** Verify that connected components work together.","source_line":1062},{"source_id":"GOV-08-005","source_section":"GOV-08","source_kind":"acceptance_gate","source_text":"**Security:** Verify permissions, isolation, credentials, data protection and action policies.","source_line":1063},{"source_id":"GOV-08-006","source_section":"GOV-08","source_kind":"acceptance_gate","source_text":"**External machinery:** Integrate available providers, hardware and protocols. Identify unavailable external dependencies explicitly.","source_line":1064},{"source_id":"GOV-08-007","source_section":"GOV-08","source_kind":"acceptance_gate","source_text":"**Acceptance testing:** Define and pass a test for every requirement.","source_line":1065},{"source_id":"GOV-08-008","source_section":"GOV-08","source_kind":"acceptance_gate","source_text":"**Operational readiness:** Verify installation, backup, recovery, monitoring, updates and maintenance.","source_line":1066},{"source_id":"GOV-08-009","source_section":"GOV-08","source_kind":"acceptance_gate","source_text":"**Build freeze:** Close capability expansion only when all approved requirements meet their completion criteria.","source_line":1067},{"source_id":"GOV-08-010","source_section":"GOV-08","source_kind":"acceptance_gate","source_text":"**Polishing and release:** Continue with bug fixes, performance, reliability, integration, UX and release preparation.","source_line":1068},{"source_id":"GOV-11-001","source_section":"GOV-11","source_kind":"progress_reporting","source_text":"What you inspected.","source_line":1229},{"source_id":"GOV-11-002","sou